content.text:
20 towers → victory with 4 lives. 15 towers → defeat. That's a decent difficulty curve. Maybe slightly too hard but acceptable. A human can optimize placement/upgrade; should be fine.

One issue: the AI with 20 towers ended with 1169 gold unspent because plan exhausted. It could have upgraded the last towers more (all max? maybe 15 max +5 low). With 1169 it could build 10 more pulse. So a human would have an easier time. Fine.

Now test endless generation: after victory, continueEndless, tick some waves. Later.

Next: implement mobile two-step placement and maybe a wave intel panel? Let's prioritize usability.

Mobile placement two-step:
- Add state.pendingCell (or use state.hover + a locked flag).
- In handleClick: if buildType and coarse pointer mode and no pendingCell or pendingCell != cell → set pendingCell = {cx,cy}; updateUI; return (don't build). If same cell tapped again → tryBuild.
- Add a mobile place bar with buttons "BUILD" and "CANCEL", visible when pendingCell.
- On desktop, immediate.
- Confirm button calls tryBuild(pendingCell.cx,cy); pendingCell=null.
- Cancel clears pendingCell.
- Ghost draws at pendingCell (instead of hover) on mobile.
- updateUI updates bar text and disabled state.

Detect mobile: `window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches` at load; or width<=760. Use `const coarse = window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;` and also viewport width <=760. Set state.coarse = coarse || window.innerWidth <= 760; update on resize maybe.

In render drawGhost uses s.hover; change to `const cell = s.pendingCell || s.hover`. Also drawHoverCell maybe.

Add DOM:
<div class="place-bar" id="placeBar" hidden>
  <span id="placeText">Place Pulse · 60g</span>
  <button id="placeConfirm">BUILD</button>
  <button id="placeCancel">CANCEL</button>
</div>
Position absolute bottom 104px (above wave button? wave button bottom 10 right 10, bar full width bottom 100). On mobile, full width with buttons; on desktop hidden (CSS display none via media query? We can show only when coarse class on body). Add body class `touch` when coarse. CSS `.place-bar{display:none}` and `body.touch .place-bar:not([hidden]){display:flex}`. Desktop uses immediate building so bar never shown.

But wave button on mobile when placing is bottom right; place bar bottom 104 might overlap? Wave button height 88 at bottom 10 → top at 98; place bar bottom 104 sits above. Good. The tower panel hidden during build (selectedTower cleared). Fine.

Confirm/cancel buttons touch-friendly (min-height 40px).

Also after selecting build type on mobile, the hint at top says "tap a free cell"; with pending, hint hidden? Keep hint showing instructions, bar appears after first tap. Update hint text when pending: "Tap BUILD to confirm". Or hide hint when bar visible. Use updateUI.

Implementation details:

state.pendingCell = null; reset in resetGame, selectBuild, selectTower, after build/cancel.

handleClick:
```
if (state.buildType) {
  if (existing) { selectTower(existing); return; }
  if (state.touch) {
    if (state.pendingCell && state.pendingCell.cx===cx && state.pendingCell.cy===cy) {
      tryBuild(cx,cy);
    } else {
      state.pendingCell={cx,cy};
      state.hover={cx,cy};
      sound.play('click');
      updateUI();
    }
    return;
  }
  tryBuild(cx,cy); return;
}
```
tryBuild success: clear pendingCell.
If invalid cell (path) → toast; pending maybe keep? Set pendingCell only if buildable? Better allow pending on any cell and show red ghost; confirm disabled. But selecting a path cell gives feedback. Let pending set; bar shows "CANNOT BUILD HERE"; confirm disabled. Good.

updateUI:
```
const p = state.pendingCell;
if (p && state.buildType && state.touch) {
  const ok = C.isBuildable(...) && !occupied && gold>=cost;
  placeBar.hidden=false;
  placeText.textContent = ok? `PLACE ${name} · ${cost}g` : !buildable? 'ROUTE BLOCKED' : occupied? 'CELL OCCUPIED' : 'NOT ENOUGH GOLD';
  confirm.disabled=!ok; cancel...
  hint hidden? yes.
} else placeBar.hidden=true;
```
Ghost uses pending cell.

Cancel button clears pending and buildType? "CANCEL" should cancel placement entirely (clear buildType and pending). Or just pending? Probably cancel build mode. Add two buttons: BUILD and CANCEL. Cancel clears both.

Tapping a different cell moves pending. Good.

Selecting a tower while pending: existing tower click selects and clears buildType/pending.

Also `selectBuild` clears pending.

Draw ghost uses `s.pendingCell || s.hover`; and hover highlight. For mobile, pendingCell remains after build? clear.

Add CSS.

Let's implement.

